\subsection{Setup}
We evaluate four backbones spanning generation paradigm, codec, and tokenizer: the autoregressive LLM-based Sarashina2.2-TTS~\cite{sarashina2026tts} and CosyVoice~2~\cite{du2024cosyvoice2}, the diffusion model Irodori-TTS-500M-v3~\cite{aratako2026irodori}, and the encoder--decoder T5Gemma-TTS~\cite{arata2026t5gemmatts}. The recipe --- text set, LoRA configuration and training procedure --- was developed on Sarashina2.2-TTS and applied to the other three without per-backbone tuning; teacher prompting and teacher-take selection differ by backbone as \S\ref{sec:method} states, and on CosyVoice~2 the number of teacher voices was chosen by a rule fixed in advance (\S\ref{sec:reftab}). Evaluation words are disjoint from training words by construction.

Reading is scored as canonicalized target-word hit under one pass of a kana-constrained ASR (kana-whisper, released with~\cite{sarashina2026tts}); the Kana column of Table~\ref{tab:reading} is the check that the ASR reads each backbone's output ($\ge 0.82$ on all four).

\textbf{Reference voices.} Zero-shot backbones need a reference prompt, and each ships a different default; measuring each under its own prompt makes the columns incomparable. Every result on the test half, and every listening and naturalness stimulus, is therefore synthesized under one of $42$ held-out voices per item, assigned by hash before any audio existed: $42$ ReazonSpeech~\cite{yin2023reazonspeech} speakers chosen as cluster centroids of a speaker-embedding space, none of which appears in any training or teacher-generation stage. Two ITA-corpus speakers were used only to select among the CosyVoice~2 adapters (\S\ref{sec:reftab}).

\subsection{Rejecting degenerate output, identically in every arm}
\label{sec:guard}
Every backbone occasionally emits non-speech (silence, a repeated mora, a run to the token limit), which a reading metric would score as misses. One guard is applied identically to every arm: a take is rejected if it is under $0.5$\,s, reaches the generator's length cap, is silent, is too quiet to hear, or transcribes as fewer than two morae or as one mora repeated six times or more; the seed is bumped, and the \emph{first} valid take is kept. Never the best of several --- that would be a take selection; the retry count is recorded per item.

Sarashina degenerates on the first take to $0.6\%$ of tagged items, compared with $0.9\%$ in plain kana and $0.9\%$ unedited, and guarding moves its tagged reading accuracy by less than one point ($0.828$ to $0.821$).

Output too quiet to hear (peak below $0.05$) is the one failure that redrawing does not cure: it persists in $4.1\%$ of tagged and $2.8\%$ of unedited T5Gemma items, and under $1\%$ on CosyVoice~2, never on Sarashina or Irodori.

